# Aesir

Agentic development platform that automates software workflows - from feature request to shipped code.

## Architecture

### 3-Layer Structure

```
Agents (dev-agent, product-agent)
   ↓ uses
Integrations (@aesir/integration-linear, @aesir/integration-github, @aesir/integration-slack)
   ↓ uses
Platform (config, logging, state, temporal)
```

**Dependency rules:**
- Agents communicate with Integrations via HTTP/MCP (no direct imports)
- Integrations import from Platform only
- Platform imports nothing from Agents or Integrations
- Agents import from Platform and Common only

## Local Development

```bash
docker compose up              # Start all services
docker compose up -d           # Start in background
docker compose watch           # Hot reload mode
docker compose down            # Stop all services
```

### Service Ports

| Service | Port | URL |
|---------|------|-----|
| PostgreSQL | 5432 | localhost:5432 |
| Temporal gRPC | 7233 | localhost:7233 |
| Temporal UI | 8080 | http://localhost:8080 |
| Linear Integration | 3001 | http://localhost:3001 |
| GitHub Integration | 3002 | http://localhost:3002 |
| Slack Integration | 3003 | http://localhost:3003 |
| Dev Agent | 3004 | http://localhost:3004 |

## Testing

```bash
pnpm test                 # Run all tests
pnpm test:fast           # Skip integration tests
pnpm test:integration    # Integration tests only
pnpm test:coverage       # With coverage report
```

## Key Patterns

### Factory Functions with Dependency Injection

```typescript
export function createMyService(options: MyServiceOptions): MyService {
  const { db, logger } = options;
  return {
    async doWork() { /* ... */ },
    async health() { /* ... */ },
    async close() { /* ... */ },
  };
}
```

### Result Types for Error Handling

```typescript
import { ok, err, ResultAsync } from "neverthrow";

function fetchData(): ResultAsync<Data, ApiError> {
  return ResultAsync.fromPromise(
    api.fetch(),
    (e) => new ApiError("Fetch failed", { cause: e })
  );
}
```

### Zod Validation at Boundaries

```typescript
const ConfigSchema = z.object({
  port: z.number().default(3000),
  apiKey: z.string().min(1),
});

const config = ConfigSchema.parse(rawInput);
```

## MCP Layer

Each integration exposes MCP tools at `/mcp/*`:
- Linear: http://localhost:3001/mcp/*
- GitHub: http://localhost:3002/mcp/*
- Slack: http://localhost:3003/mcp/*

Headers:
- `X-Agent-ID` - Required for tool invocation
- `X-Correlation-ID` - Optional, for request tracing

**Agent Usage:**
```typescript
import { callMcpTool } from "@aesir/agents";

const issue = await callMcpTool({
  integration: "linear",
  tool: "get_issue",
  params: { issueId: "ABC-123" },
  agentId: "dev-agent",
});
```

## Package Structure

```
packages/
├── agents/              # @aesir/agents
├── integrations/
│   ├── linear/          # @aesir/integration-linear
│   ├── github/          # @aesir/integration-github
│   ├── slack/           # @aesir/integration-slack
│   └── src/             # @aesir/integrations (legacy)
├── platform/            # @aesir/platform
├── observability/       # @aesir/observability
└── common/              # @aesir/common
```

## Gotchas

- Use pnpm (not npm) for package management
- Use `--legacy-peer-deps` for npm if needed (LangChain conflicts)
- Docker Compose watch rebuilds entire container on file changes
- Each integration has its own database schema namespace (linear.*, github.*, slack.*)
